==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|rectifier||to make straight|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|rēctificāre||make right|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|rēctus||straight|lang=la}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛktəˌfaɪ/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|rectif|i|ed}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[correct]] or [[amend]] something.
# {{context|transitive|chemistry|lang=en}} To [[purify]] or [[refine]], especially by [[distillation]].
# {{context|transitive|electronics|lang=en}} To [[convert]] [[alternating current]] into [[direct current]].

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:repair]]

